                <head>[Inclosure 1.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[Instructions to Diplomatic Officers, sec. 33.]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Notarial services</hi>.—The existing statute authorizes
                    secretaries of embassy or legation to administer oaths, take depositions, and
                    generally to perform notarial acts. (R. S., sec. 1750.) This statute is not
                    construed by the Department of State as mandatory on a secretary of embassy or
                    legation. He is at liberty to act or refuse to act, but it is thought that he
                    will feel it his duty to accommodate persons desiring his services in a notarial
                    capacity. When so acting he is entirely outside of his official duties, and his
                    compensation, if he receives any, will belong to him personally.</p>
            </div>
